<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This method was able to closely mimic the patterns of the training dataset in some samples but still failed in other instances. It often does not produce proper claims, as it focuses solely on optimizing the METEOR score.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">T5-base (LoRA, fine-tuned)</h5>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">METEOR Score: 0.3054, described in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 2.1 LoRA fine-tuning of Flan-T5 Base ‣ 2 Approaches: Fine-Tuning and Prompting ‣ UNH at CheckThat! 2025: Fine-tuning Vs Prompting in Claim Extraction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
